      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel exhausted when you feel like the old self is gone and the effort to recapture it feels futile. Acknowledging that the mask has slipped and that the previous version of you is gone is a huge, albeit painful, realization. Instead of fighting to find someone who has dissolved, perhaps you could allow yourself to explore what this quiet emptiness *is* without the pressure of needing it to be something vibrant. Sometimes, the deepest change begins when we stop trying to force a return to the past.",
